# Career Content Sync

When editing portfolio career content, keep the career advisor knowledge base aligned.

## LinkedIn audit

```bash
node .cursor/career/scripts/audit-linkedin.mjs
```

Writes `.cursor/career/audits/YYYY-MM-DD-linkedin.md`. Refresh `.cursor/career/.cache/linkedin-snapshot.md` for full skills/experience parsing.

## After changes to matched files

1. Run from repo root:

```bash
node .cursor/career/scripts/sync-career-profile.mjs
```

2. Verify `.cursor/career/profile.md` reflects the updates.

3. If narrative positioning changed (headline, about, achievements), also update:
   - `.cursor/career/voice.md` — if tone/positioning shifted
   - `.cursor/career/achievements.md` — if new metrics or STAR stories
   - `.cursor/career/linkedin-baseline.md` — if LinkedIn was updated to match

4. If resume PDF changed (`web/public/resume/`), flag consistency check:
   - Titles and dates vs `profile.md`
   - Frontend vs full-stack positioning vs target roles

## Source of truth hierarchy

| Layer | Location | Role |
|-------|----------|------|
| Public portfolio | `web/messages/`, `web/lib/data/` | Canonical for site |
| Career KB | `.cursor/career/profile.md` | Auto-synced facts for agents |
| Resume PDF | `web/public/resume/` | Formal CV — read on demand |
| Private goals | `.cursor/career/goals.md` | User-maintained targets |

Do not duplicate resume content into markdown — avoids drift.
